git init
→ usage: start git in project

git clone <repo-link>   (If other project vennu na)
→ usage: download project from GitHub

git status
→ usage: check changes

git add .
→ usage: add all files

git commit -m "message"
→ usage: save changes

git push
→ usage: upload code to GitHub

git pull
→ usage: get latest code from team

git remote add origin <repo-link>   (other person project ha connect panna)
→ usage: connect to GitHub

git branch
→ usage: see branches

git checkout -b branch-name
→ usage: create new branch

git checkout branch-name
→ usage: switch branch

git push -u origin branch-name
→ usage: upload new branch

git merge branch-name
→ usage: merge branch


✅ Daily use (important)
git pull
git add .
git commit -m "work"
git push

=====================================================================================================
  if your project want to uplaod



  # Step 1: Go to project folder
  cd path/to/your/project

  # Step 2: Start git
  git init
  → usage: initialize git

  # Step 3: Add all files
  git add .
  → usage: add all project files

  # Step 4: Commit
  git commit -m "first commit"
  → usage: save project

  # Step 5: Connect to GitHub
  git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo.git
  → usage: link GitHub repo

  # Step 6: Push code
  git branch -M main
  git push -u origin main
  → usage: upload project to GitHub



